; `listenable-sources` returns the (sorted) available input-device names as
; a `[String]`, so you can `start-listening-from` a device by index rather
; than spelling its name. Test IO managers report no devices, so the list
; is empty here — this pins the plumbing (building the `[String]`,
; array-length, printing) on both runtimes.
@cpu
(defn main []
  (let [sources (listenable-sources)]
    (print (array-length sources))
    (print sources)))
